
                                         KESTREL
                                A ligand-field program for
                              3d transition-metal complexes

                   ----------------------------------------------------
                   |        Version: 1.0.0, Copyright (c) 2026        |
                   | Department of Chemistry, University of York (UK) |
                   ----------------------------------------------------

    References:
        1.  Nunn, George (2023) Development of a contemporary ligand-field
            program for 3d transition-metal complexes. PhD thesis,
            University of York.
        2.  P. Comba, G. Nunn, F. Scherz and P. H. Walton, Faraday Discuss., 2021, 234, 232-244.
        3.  S. Mace, B. S. Grace, A. Goodfellow, M. A. Bates, M. A. Halcrow, P. H .Walton,
            Y. Xu and B. N. Nguyen, Inorg. Chem. Front., 2026, 13 (17), 7301-7315.


    Contributors:
        - George Nunn: Former PhD student in the PHW group.
        - Ben Grace: PhD student in the PHW group.
        - Martin Bates: PhD project supervisor.
        - Paul Walton: PhD project supervisor.


                                 *** PARAMETER SPACE ***

=========================================================================================
                                     INPUT
=========================================================================================
MetalAssignment:
----------------
Field                Value
-------------------  -------------------------------------
d_electrons          7
racah_b              Varied(value=[900.0, 1000.0, 1100.0])
racah_c              Fixed(value=4223.0)
spin_orbit_coupling  Fixed(value=0.0)
kiso                 Fixed(value=1.0)

LigandAssignment:
-----------------
Field    Value
-------  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
name     Cl
esigma   Varied(value=[5000.0, 5250.0, 5500.0, 5750.0, 6000.0, 6250.0, 6500.0, 6750.0, 7000.0, 7250.0, 7500.0])
epix     Varied(value=[1500.0, 1650.0, 1800.0, 1950.0, 2100.0, 2250.0, 2400.0, 2550.0, 2700.0, 2850.0, 3000.0])
epiy     Link(object_reference='ligand.Cl.epix', link_type=<LinkType.LINEAR: 'linear'>, link_arguments={'gradient': 1.0, 'constant': 0.0})
edxy     Fixed(value=0.0)
edx2y2   Fixed(value=0.0)
eds      Fixed(value=0.0)

